// Test: plugins/build_state_round_trip
// Plugin Contracts v2 — exercises the _build_state_get + string == "" +
// _build_state_set sequence that frame.ui 2.12.0 uses in expand_component.
//
// Regression: HYDRATE_AUTO — UI-bearing apps hit a wasm `unreachable` trap
// when the plugin's compiled Clean code runs through the build_state bridge
// sequence. See compiler-frame-ui-v2-followup-trap-and-silent-orchestrator.md.
//
// Compiled as a plugin via `cln compile --target=plugin`. Loaded by
// tests/test_plugin_build_state_round_trip.rs with the build_state bridges
// registered. The test calls `expand_block` twice and asserts no trap.
//
// Bridges are declared in the sibling plugin.toml's [bridge] section with
// `expand_strings = true`, matching the canonical contract in
// foundation/platform-architecture/function-registry.toml. This is the same
// declaration path frame.ui uses — the compiler reads plugin.toml, expands
// each "string" param into (ptr, len) pairs on the host import side, and
// generates wrapper functions that adapt LP-pointer call sites in the .cln
// source to the raw import. An `external:` block here would emit the
// pre-canonical LP-pointer signature (single i32 per string, void mapped to
// i32 return) and disagree with the host adapter — the exact mismatch that
// closed CMP-PLUGIN-ABI-BUILD-STATE-SET-MISMATCH.

functions:
	string expand_block(string name, string attrs, string body)
		string current = _build_state_get("test:key")
		if current == ""
			_build_state_set("test:key", "first")
		else
			_build_state_set("test:key", current + ";next")
		return body
